# BFCL Data Directory Structure Rules

## File Placement
- Place official BFCL benchmark datasets (BFCL_v4_*.json) at data/ root
- Place all Python/shell scripts in data/scripts/
- Place generated training data in data/generated/sft/ or data/generated/rl/
- Place evaluation results in data/generated/evaluation/
- Place visualization outputs (PNG, SVG) in data/outputs/plots/
- Place data format templates in data/templates/

## Naming Conventions
- Benchmark files: BFCL_v4_{category}.json
- SFT datasets: bfcl_sft_{version_or_name}.json
- RL data: rl_{type}_{optional_suffix}.json
- Evaluation: {metric}_results.json or trajectory_reward_results.json
- Comparison: compare_{a}_vs_{b}.json
- Plots: {metric}_histogram.png or {name}_chart.png

## Script Execution
- Run shell scripts from data/scripts/ directory: cd data/scripts && ./build_sft_data.sh
- Scripts use relative paths from scripts/ to access parent data directory
- Local config paths are in config.local.sh (not tracked by git)
